      "maturity.radarTitle": "Distribution by domain",
      "maturity.radarLead": "Gap between current level and target (scale 1–5)",
      "maturity.whyTitle": "Why this score",
      "maturity.whyScore": "The {score}/100 index ({level}) is not a consulting grade: open findings subtract. This scan has {c} critical, {h} high, {m} medium, {l} low and {i} info. Each critical pulls hard; an info barely moves. That is why a single SQLi on login can leave IAM at 1.0 even if the rest of the radar looks «green».",
      "maturity.howUp": "To move up a level, close the weakest domains first ({domains}). A 4.0 target on an axis means: no open criticals or highs on that control. Re-scan afterwards; if the radar does not move, the finding is still open or it is not classified on that domain.",
      "maturity.vsFair": "Do not confuse this index with the FAIR-lite grade on the «Exposure index» dossier. FAIR summarizes business risk (exposure × threat × impact) for leadership. Maturity summarizes control capability per domain (1–5) for the CISO. You can have FAIR C and Initial maturity at once: lots of surface and few demonstrable controls.",
      "maturity.domainsExplain": "What each domain measures and why it looks like this",
      "maturity.domainHits": "Findings that pull this axis down",
      "maturity.domainClear": "No finding in this scan maps to this domain. That does not certify the control: it only says the playbook did not see a failure here.",
      "maturity.whyIam": "Identity: login, sessions, cookies, MFA and IdP (Entra/Workspace/SAML). SQLi on login or cookies without flags flatten this domain.",
      "maturity.whyNet": "Network and perimeter: TLS, headers, SPF/DMARC, ports. A domain without DMARC or CSP drops this axis even if the rest looks healthy.",
      "maturity.whyData": "Data: secrets in code, SQL, backups, listable buckets. A critical here is what hurts most under GDPR.",
      "maturity.whyIr": "Incident response: RCE, file inclusion, uploads. If the attacker can run code, IR has no margin.",
      "maturity.whyAware": "Awareness and deploy hygiene: DVWA, debug, display_errors. It flags environments that should not be public.",
      "maturity.whyAssets": "Inventory: directory listing, robots, document root. Surface the team had not mapped.",
